@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+#!/usr/bin/env bash
+set -u
+
+if [[ "$#" -lt 2 ]]; then
+  echo "usage: run_logged.sh LABEL COMMAND [ARG ...]" >&2
+  exit 64
+fi
+
+label="$1"
+shift
+log="/audit-output/evidence/logs/${label}.log"
+
+{
+  printf 'WORKDIR: %s\n' "$PWD"
+  printf 'COMMAND:'
+  printf ' %q' "$@"
+  printf '\n'
+  printf 'START_UTC: '
+  date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'
+  "$@"
+  status=$?
+  printf 'EXIT_STATUS: %d\n' "$status"
+  printf 'END_UTC: '
+  date -u '+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ'
+  exit "$status"
+} >"$log" 2>&1

All seven audit stages are complete. REVIEW.md and reviewer evidence are written, cited, and marker-validated.
  ✓ Read mandated Kit skill instructions and establish audit workflow
  ✓ Validate input/provenance integrity and semantics-mode boundary
  ✓ Check program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Rebuild semantics/proof cleanly and execute all positive claims
  ✓ Audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and every local rule
  ✓ Create and run a fresh meaningful false mutation
  ✓ Account for assumptions, write REVIEW.md, and issue verdict
